  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal contract obligations in Michigan are $168M for FY2027 to date. The federal government made 10,704 awards in the state, with an average award size of $15.7K. Obligations fell 98.2% year over year. The annual series shows a steep drop from prior full fiscal years: FY22 obligations were $12.9B, FY23 obligations were $12B, FY24 obligations were $11B, FY25 obligations were $8.9B, and FY26 obligations were $9.4B. The Department of Veterans Affairs led buying in FY2027 to date with $83.9M in obligations, followed by the General Services Administration with $50.2M and the Department of Agriculture with $14.5M. DANIELS BUILDING CO INC is the top vendor in FY2027 to date with $23.4M in obligations, followed by FCA US LLC with $19.6M and FORD MOTOR CO with $12.1M. Automobile Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations in FY2027 to date at $24.3M, with Electrical Contractors and Other Wiring Installation Contractors close behind at $23.7M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did federal contract spending in Michigan change this year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 98.2% year over year. Annual obligations moved from $12.9B in FY22 down to $9.4B in FY26, and they are $168M in FY27 to date. The number of awards in FY27 to date is 10,704, with an average award size of $15.7K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries dominate Michigan federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in FY2027 to date with $83.9M in obligations. The General Services Administration follows with $50.2M and the Department of Agriculture with $14.5M. Automobile Manufacturing leads industries in FY2027 to date at $24.3M, with Electrical Contractors and Other Wiring Installation Contractors at $23.7M."
      }
    ]
  },
